    "q-160355": {
      "dom_id": "step-q160355",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 20%=14,$ then $\\,\\boxed{}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The part is $14,$ the percentage is $20%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $20%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =14÷20% \\\\  & =14÷\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =14\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =14\\times 5 \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
